    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0785" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/370: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-11-07T13:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>54. Department’s 44, October 7, 5 p.m. In reply to note October 14, Acting
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs insists that a prorogation of treaty November 5,
                        1923,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d603-f1"/> was the reply of the Spanish
                    Government to the first proposal and that prorogation on May 5th last was the
                    reply of the Spanish Government to Department’s second proposal, neither draft
                    being considered satisfactory.</p>
                <p>I should appreciate Department’s sending at once draft of a purely commercial
                    treaty containing irreducible minimum and hope that it can be cabled, as knowing
                    circumstances here I think that the matter should be presented within a few
                    weeks.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
